  "archiveQualityHelp": "How the archive keeps the quality",
  "archiveQualityTitle": "How the archive keeps the quality",
  "archiveQualityIntro": "A master copy takes the place of the original, so it has to look the same. It is also there to save space, so it should weigh no more than that quality needs. Getting both right is one of the main aims of VidCtrl.",
  "archiveQualityXpsnrValue": "42 dB",
  "archiveQualityXpsnr": "A measure of how far a copy is from its original, weighing each difference by how visible it is. From 42 dB, no loss is visible. The bar is strict: on grainy footage, no difference shows at 41 dB either.",
  "archiveQualityVmaf": "Netflix's measure, which rates a copy on a scale up to 100 the way viewers would. From 95, no difference shows even side by side, and a few points lower it is still hard to spot.",
  "archiveQualityTunedTitle": "Measured, not guessed",
  "archiveQualityTuned": "For each way of encoding the archive offers, on the processor, NVIDIA graphics or a Mac, the settings were chosen separately: the smallest file that reaches these bars even on hard footage. Ordinary videos have a margin.",
  "archiveQualityCheckedTitle": "Checked before every release",
